<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office for the Friday to Sunday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final data are due Monday. (Rank last week in parentheses).</p>
<p>    1 (*) Beavis and Butt-head Do America .. $20.5 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Jerry Maguire .................... $13.4 million</p>
<p>    3 (3) 101 Dalmatians ...................  $6.8 million</p>
<p>    4 (*) Scream ...........................  $6.3 million</p>
<p>    5 (*) One Fine Day .....................  $6.1 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) The Preacher's Wife ..............  $5.3 million</p>
<p>    7 (2) Mars Attacks! ....................  $4.7 million</p>
<p>    8 (6) Jingle All the Way ...............  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    9 (*) My Fellow Americans ..............  $2.8 million</p>
<p>   10 (5) Daylight .........................  $2.3 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Beavis and Butt-head Do America&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..  &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. &quot;101 Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;The Preacher's Wife&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co..  &quot;Scream&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Disney. &quot;One Fine Day&quot; and &quot;Jingle All the Way&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..  &quot;Mars Attacks!&quot; and &quot;My Fellow Americans&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. &quot;Daylight&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
